# PRD: Freebeez Platform - Unified Free Service Management System

## Introduction

Freebeez is a platform designed to programmatically acquire and manage multiple free services from various sources. The platform automates the process of discovering, signing up for, and managing free services while handling account rotation, rate limiting, and seamless integration. The system enables power users to leverage a wide range of free tools through a single unified interface while the backend handles the complexity of multi-account management and service connectivity.

## Goals

- Automate the acquisition of free service accounts using temporary emails and CAPTCHA solving
- Implement account rotation and proxy management to respect rate limits and avoid bans
- Provide a unified interface for managing multiple third-party services
- Enable seamless integration of new services through modular connection modules
- Achieve successful automated account creation for 80% of supported services
- Aggregate 100+ free services in the initial release

## User Stories

### US-001: Service Discovery and Aggregation
**Description:** As a power user, I want to browse and discover free services from various sources so that I can find tools that meet my needs.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] System scrapes GitHub "free service/api" lists and other "tool aggregator" sites
- [ ] Services are categorized by type (development, productivity, design, etc.)
- [ ] Search functionality allows filtering by category, popularity, or keywords
- [ ] Each service entry includes description, URL, and integration status
- [ ] Typecheck passes
- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill

### US-002: Automated Account Registration
**Description:** As a power user, I want the system to automatically register for free services on my behalf so that I don't need to manually create accounts.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] System identifies signup forms and fills them with temporary email/password
- [ ] Integration with temporary email services (MailSlurp or similar) for verification
- [ ] CAPTCHA solving integration (2Captcha or similar) for automated handling
- [ ] Fallback mechanism to request user input when automation fails
- [ ] Created accounts are stored securely in the database
- [ ] Typecheck passes

### US-003: Account Rotation and Rate Limit Management
**Description:** As a power user, I want the system to automatically rotate between multiple accounts of the same service so that I can respect rate limits and avoid being banned.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Database schema tracks usage count and limits per account
- [ ] Algorithm selects least recently used account that hasn't exceeded limits
- [ ] Daily reset mechanism for usage counters
- [ ] Notification system alerts when all accounts reach limits
- [ ] Typecheck passes

### US-004: Proxy and User-Agent Rotation
**Description:** As a power user, I want the system to rotate proxies and user-agents during automation so that my activities remain undetected.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Integration with proxy rotation system (lists of proxies from providers)
- [ ] Random user-agent rotation during browser sessions
- [ ] Persistent browser profiles to maintain consistency
- [ ] Automatic fallback when proxy fails
- [ ] Typecheck passes

### US-005: Secure Credential Storage
**Description:** As a power user, I want my service credentials to be stored securely so that my accounts remain protected.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Credentials encrypted using industry-standard encryption
- [ ] Secure session management with secure cookies
- [ ] Regular credential rotation capability
- [ ] Audit logging for credential access
- [ ] Typecheck passes

### US-006: Unified Service Interface
**Description:** As a power user, I want a single interface to access all connected services so that I can manage everything from one place.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Dashboard showing all connected services and their status
- [ ] Quick access buttons to individual service interfaces
- [ ] Centralized activity feed showing recent actions across services
- [ ] Bulk management tools for connected services
- [ ] Typecheck passes
- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill

### US-007: Modular Connection Architecture
**Description:** As a developer, I want a modular system for connecting to different services so that new integrations can be added easily.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Plugin architecture for different service types
- [ ] Standardized API for common service operations
- [ ] Configuration files defining service-specific parameters
- [ ] Easy addition of new service connectors without code changes
- [ ] Typecheck passes

### US-008: Service Interconnectivity
**Description:** As a power user, I want to link data and workflows across different services so that I can create powerful automation chains.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Ability to sync data between connected services
- [ ] Workflow builder for creating cross-service automations
- [ ] Event triggers from one service can initiate actions in another
- [ ] Visual representation of service connections
- [ ] Typecheck passes
- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill

## Functional Requirements

- FR-1: The system must provide a service discovery module that aggregates free services from GitHub and other sources
- FR-2: The system must implement automated registration workflows using temporary emails and CAPTCHA solving
- FR-3: The system must track account usage and implement rotation algorithms to respect rate limits
- FR-4: The system must rotate proxies and user-agents during automation to avoid detection
- FR-5: The system must securely encrypt and store service credentials
- FR-6: The system must provide a unified dashboard interface for all connected services
- FR-7: The system must support a plugin architecture for easy addition of new service integrations
- FR-8: The system must enable data synchronization and workflow creation between services
- FR-9: The system must implement notification mechanisms for manual intervention when automation fails

## Non-Goals

- Building custom implementations of existing services (only integration)
- Providing paid service management (focus on free services only)
- Creating a marketplace for services (just discovery and connection)
- Implementing complex business logic beyond account management
- Supporting services that require payment information during signup

## Design Considerations

- UI/UX: Clean dashboard interface with service cards showing status and quick actions
- Security: Zero-knowledge architecture where possible, with client-side encryption
- Scalability: Microservices architecture to handle multiple concurrent automation tasks
- Reliability: Fallback mechanisms for when automation fails, with graceful degradation

## Technical Considerations

- Backend: Node.js/Express or Python/FastAPI for handling automation workflows
- Database: MongoDB or PostgreSQL for storing account profiles, limits, and rotation states
- Browser Automation: Puppeteer/Playwright for services without APIs, with stealth capabilities
- Queue System: Bull (Redis-based) or Celery for async automation tasks
- Authentication: JWT-based with secure session management
- Proxy Management: Integration with proxy providers and rotation algorithms
- CAPTCHA Solving: Integration with services like 2Captcha for automated solving
- Temporary Emails: Integration with MailSlurp or similar for verification

## Success Metrics

- Successfully register and verify 80% of attempted free service accounts
- Support 100+ unique free services in the first quarter
- Achieve 99% uptime for core automation services
- Reduce manual intervention in account creation to under 10% of attempts
- Support 1000+ concurrent users performing automation tasks

## Open Questions

- How should the system handle services that require phone number verification?
- What is the optimal balance between automation speed and detection avoidance?
- Should there be a premium tier for additional features or higher limits?
- How will the system handle terms of service changes from integrated services?

